Attempting to write a toy example with Bazel, Pybind, Pytorch/Libtorch fails with the following error on import of the custom library. This setup works fine with Cmake, but attempting to port that over to Bazel, I think i might be missing some step?
import libTest
undefined symbol: _ZN3c1019UndefinedTensorImpl10_singletonE

The Bazel WORKSPACE:
http_archive(
    name = "pytorch_cpu",
    build_file = "//tools:pytorch_cpu.BUILD",
    sha256 = "6b99edc046f37ad37a3b04dc86663895f10c362af09fdd10884f30360d0ba023",
    urls = [
        "https://download.pytorch.org/libtorch/cpu/libtorch-cxx11-abi-shared-with-deps-1.9.0%2Bcpu.zip"
    ],
)

The Bazel Build file
package(default_visibility = ["//visibility:public"])

cc_library(
    name = "pytorch_cpu",
    includes = ["libtorch/include/torch/csrc/api/include", "libtorch/include"],
    hdrs = glob([
      "libtorch/include/**"
    ]),
    srcs = glob([
      "libtorch/lib/*",
    ]),
)

And the toy example in Pybind
#include <pybind11/pybind11.h>
#include <pybind11/stl.h>
#include <pybind11/numpy.h>
#include <pybind11/pytypes.h>


#include <torch/torch.h>
#include <torch/csrc/utils/pybind.h>


namespace py = pybind11;

torch::Tensor myUsefulMethod() 
{
  return torch::zeros({62,1});
}

PYBIND11_MODULE(libTest, m) {

  m.def("myUsefulMethod", &myUsefulMethod, "myUsefulMethod");

  #ifdef VERSION_INFO
    m.attr("__version__") = VERSION_INFO;
  #else
    m.attr("__version__") = "dev";
  #endif
}

#endif

built as
cc_library(
    name = "Test",
    srcs = ["Test.cpp"],
    deps = [
        "@pybind11",
        "@pytorch_cpu"
    ],
)

What might be the issue here? This setup seems to work fine in Cmake, but gives the undefined tensor impl error in my bazel setup. Just to note, Libtorch 1.9 binaries were pulled from that above link and pytorch 1.9 installed in it's own pyenv using the default pip install instructions. But they are certainly the same version
cc @malfet @seemethere @walterddr @yf225 @glaringlee @zou3519

