🐛 Bug
If min is omitted In torch.clamp, an output onnx file is invalid.
To Reproduce
Steps to reproduce the behavior:

docker run -it  ubuntu:18.04 -v ${PWD}:/work /bin/bash
apt update && apt install -y python3-pip
pip3 install torch onnx
python3 gen_onnx.py  # gen_onnx.py is the following file

With torch 1.9.0, the following model produces an invalid onnx file:
import torch
import onnx

FILENAME = 'model.onnx'


class Model(torch.nn.Module):
    def forward(self, x0):
        x = torch.clamp(x0, max=6)
        return x

torch.onnx.export(Model(), torch.randn(5, 5), FILENAME, opset_version=11)
model = onnx.load(FILENAME)
onnx.checker.check_model(model)
print(model)

